<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 28.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended June 28</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     365	   1.96     558200  203.74   28.00</p>
<p>Telco		  440	   2.41     278550  122.56   28.56</p>
<p>TISCO		  183	   1.00     636800  116.53   28.49</p>
<p>ITC		    525	   2.95     174700   91.72   29.30</p>
<p>HDFC		  3710	  21.19	18140   67.30   29.78</p>
<p>Castrol		505	   2.89	85550   43.20   29.84</p>
<p>BHEL		   370	   2.14     107000   39.59   30.16</p>
<p>BSES		   235	   1.34     154650   36.34   29.73</p>
<p>ACC		   1390	   7.09	25990   36.13   26.60</p>
<p>STERLITE	     260	   1.51     119900   31.17   30.28</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 29.37 percent on an annualised basis against 21.42 percent in the previous carry forward account ended June 21.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
